entDocument()?"],["55b2baab_be99829d",37,-6,1,"Add comment on why this is needed? It appears unused?"],["a3589ca1_7fc81669",36,-6,1,"What are the equivalents to these checks in the new code? Or are you assuming this cannot happen?"],["bad53cec_5e5fc3c2",37,-6,0,"Add comment? Also, why is this a set, it appears we have one receiver only? Or is this to support a future receiver?"],["bc3cf0ed_43010bd7",37,-6,0,"Is this constructor supposed to be public?"],["c80169a8_ea9d03f3",11,-6,1,"Not public. Is this needed?"],["fd252126_77156460",36,-6,0,"This now only reports bad message, without deleting this. Is this change intentional?"],["469733a1_360bdca9",38,-5,1,"I guess this is convenient, but I feel like the right way to model this is by navigating."],["af17dbfe_63df639d",36,-5,1,"Nit: have a comment that explains why we need an explicit clear here–though this doesn't seem necessary?"],["d8b53d4d_7442aada",39,-5,1,"I might call this `AddReceiver()` instead if we support binding it more than once. (I am going to ask: is it expected that this interface can be bound more than once? The CL description talks about…"]],0,933],[7148238,20410,159,4.528,3.643,[[1,1.0,169,153]],[["346c27b9_2477fb31",40,0,1,"Remove?"],["4b64b5a8_e65f2e00",41,0,1,"Could you add a test for this?"],["5db3af38_b3185600",40,0,1,"Could you also add a test *with* activation from the handler?"],["ecb5f66b_fc0d034a",41,0,1,"Do you think it's worth moving this check to a helper function that can be reused by RequestService?"],["fbb1551a_cea6710b",36,0,1,"nit: add a comment"]],0,934],[7142063,20412,118,2.91,2.334,[[1,170]],[["2010d783_c058c7f4",41,-9,1,"```suggestion // to initiate the request in the RFH for the initiating RFH, so we look ```"],["22e42469_13d561ee",41,-8,1,"Beyond the initiator consideration above, we also don't have a guarantee that this was the current RFH in the target FrameTreeNode at the time the navigation began-- see…"],["79a9934c_ccf42abd",41,-8,1,"Hmm, this is not always true. The navigation could be initiated by a different RFH, such as another tab or a subframe that is targeting the frame that is navigating. For example, `w=window.open();…"],["afcb1180_c4af6751",41,-8,1,"nit: This is also sometimes wrong, in the case that the initiator is in a different frame or tab. This code doesn't appear to be tracking navigations in the actual initiator, only in the target frame…"],["9ccece69_d3e19a73",40,-1,0,"Optional: In a followup, you might consider adding a test that ensures the flow does not continue if the target RFH navigates to another document in the meantime, verifying the new WillStartRequest…"],["a921d33c_3250b4cd",41,-1,1,"Is it easy to write a unit test to capture this case?"],["bb6c81cf_043f4bdb",42,-1,1,"This would benefit from a comment, along the lines of: Tracks the document present in the target RenderFrameHost at the time the relevant navigation began. This will be navigated to complete the…"],["d571f601_51236805",42,-1,1,"does it matter that this is a weak_ptr? can we call this a document_ instead?"]],0,935],[7205035,20418,4,0.248,0.173,[[22,0]],[],0,936],[7127303,20427,438,7.602,6.22,[[1,0.951,171,418],[4,0.027,30,10],[23,0.022,12,8]],[["207bf6b7_f02f7d16",43,-25,1,"can't we make the fact that we are making an HTTP request (rather than a local DNS request) an implementation detail of this class (rather than move to the network manager)?"],["068a16e4_39bad7eb",44,-4,0,"Can't FetchWellKnown call into DownloadAndParseUncredialedUrl?"],["6bb9c753_e93ac76d",45,-4,0,"Hard coding dns.google here makes sense to me, specially since we could allow embedders to pick a different DNS resolver if they wanted to."],["71e0d05b_ec124f42",46,-4,0,"Can you write a test that covers when \"hostname\" has things that would break the URL, like an &? Or better yet, is there a reason why we can't take a base::Origin here instead rather than a…"],["d072b24a_cf2f1dc6",47,-4,0,"Can you assert that the request is being made to the right URL here? Specifically, I'd like to see this test break if anyone changes this value \"https://dns.google/resolve?type=txt&do=1&name=\" in the…"],["ca43b942_1ef39921",11,-1,0,"This paragraph is not valid anymore, since the CL now does go to the embedder for it and doesn't hardcode it in //content/."]],0,937],[7247728,20432,11,0.452,0.316,[[1,0.6,171,7],[7,0.4,19,4]],[],0,937],[7254603,20438,622,16.15,13.645,[[1,0.918,172,577],[23,0.049,12,28],[7,0.02,20,11],[18,0.013,15,6]],[["5d8a5e52_8b5b51ad",48,-1,0,"ditto"],["a3bb670a_6102ce0f",48,-1,0,"ditto"],["cafac087_ea7a6655",48,-1,0,"ditto"],["d8c53140_0b4e57b9",48,-1,0,"Do we need to remove this one?"],["d9191710_58155cfc",49,-1,1,"This one also expired btw, crbug.com/465390917"]],0,938],[7275842,20441,12,0.421,0.3,[[24,4]],[["497feecd_02a3f002",11,0,1,"nit: incorrect wrap"]],0,939]]}